s Biography\n\nImages Additional images\n\n## About this book\n\nIn this updated edition of a groundbreaking text, concepts such as energy return on investment (EROI) provide powerful insights into the real balance sheets that drive our \"petroleum economy\". --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n978-3-319-66219-0_Book_OnlinePDF.pdf (https://www.inist.org/Library/2018.Hall-Klitgaard.EnergyAndTheWealthOfNations.Springer.pdf)\nciteturn146search12 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 months ago; \nCharles A.S. Hall  \nKent Klitgaard  \n\n# Energy and the Wealth of Nations\n\nAn Introduction to Biophysical Economics\n\nSecond Edition\n\nSpringer--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEnergy and the Wealth of Nations : understanding the biophysical economy | WorldCat.org (https://search.worldcat.org/title/Energy-and-the-Wealth-of-Nations-%3A-understanding-the-biophysical-economy/oclc/1041780476)\nciteturn146search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.8 years ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; \n\nImage: Front cover image for Energy and the Wealth of Nations : understanding the biophysical economy\n\n# \n\nEnergy and the Wealth of Nations : understanding the biophysical economy\n\nAuthors:Charles AS Hall, Kent Klitgaard,\n\nSpringer International Publishing (Publisher)\n\n* * *\n\nPrint Book, English, 2018\n\nEdition:Second edition\n\nPublisher: Springer International Publishing, Cham, 2018--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEnergy and the Wealth of Nations: Understanding the Biophysical Economy | Springer Nature Link (https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4419-9398-4)\nciteturn146search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 15.0 years ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; \n\n# Energy and the Wealth of Nations\n\nUnderstanding the Biophysical Economy\n\n  * Textbook\n  * © 2012\n\n  * 1st edition\n  * View latest edition\n\nEnergy and the Wealth of Nations\n\n## Overview\n\nAuthors:\n    \n\n  * Charles A. S. Hall ^{0},\n  * Kent A. Klitgaard ^{1}\n\n  * Integrates energy and economics\n  * Uses predictive tools and measures, such as EROI, to show how the economy is embedded in a biophysical world subject to scientific rules and constraints\n  * Provides a fresh approach to economics for those wondering “What’s next?“ after the Great Recession and the recent increases in oil prices\n  * Assesses energy sources from the perspective of peak oil, the role of alternatives, and potential impacts such as climate change\n\n  * 81k Accesses\n\n  * 251 Citations\n\n  * 55 Altmetric\n\nThis is a preview of subscription content, to check access.\n\n## Access this book\n\nLog in via an institution\n\neBook USD 74.99\n\nPrice excludes VAT (USA)\n\nKent A. Klitgaard is Professor of Economics and the Patti McGill Peterson Professor of Social Sciences at Wells College in Aurora, New York, where he has taught since 1991. Kent received his Bachelor’s degree at San Diego State University and his Master’s and PhD at the University of New Hampshire. At Wells, he teaches a diverse array of courses including the History of Economic Thought, Political Economy, Ecological Economics, The Economics of Energy, Technology and the Labor Process, and Microeconomic Theory, and is a co-founder of the Environmental Studies Program. Kent is active in the International Society for Ecological Economics, and is a founding member of the International Society for Biophysical Economics. Recently, his interests have turned towards the degrowth movement, and he has published multiple papers on the subject for Research and Degrowth. He has two children, and is interested in the outdoors in general: from hiking to beach walking to the occasional round of golf (despite the high energy use of golf courses). Kent is a Californian who still surfs the frigidwaters of New England when he gets a chance. This is his first book.\n\n## Bibliographic information\n\n  * Book title: Energy a